Specular patch to UnRAR 7.1.0 (vendor/unrar in unrar_sys 0.5.8): passwords through the open
hook. Applied after specular-handle-io.patch.

What it changes
  dll.cpp and file.cpp. Before RAROpenArchiveEx opens an archive, it asks the open hook of
  specular-handle-io.patch for the reserved names "\x01password/0", "\x01password/1", ...;
  each answer is one byte (1..255) of the password's UTF-8, and -1 (or anything else) ends
  it. A non-empty password is converted with UtfToWide and set as the command's password,
  and the temporary copies are wiped with cleandata. file.cpp gains
  SpecularUnrarCallHook(), which calls the hook for dll.cpp.

Why
  RARSetPassword takes a C string in the locale's character set and only applies after
  RAROpenArchiveEx, which already needs the password to read encrypted headers (RAR -hp);
  the open callback would make the host answer UnRAR's questions mid-call. The hook is
  already the one channel between UnRAR and the host, and no name the hook otherwise
  serves starts with \x01, so the password needs no new entry point, never exists as a
  C string, and reaches both encrypted headers and encrypted files.

